      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/gymnogeophagus-caaguazuensis-4/",
      "html": "<p>Gymnogeophagus caaguazuensis is a larvophile maternal mouthbrooding cichlid from Paraguay. With only scarcely 9 cm of standard length (at most 12 cm in total length with the tail fin), it is one of the smallest species of the genus.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/gymnogeophagus-caaguazuensis-4/",
      "html": "<p>Paraguay. The animals offered were wild-caught.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/gymnogeophagus-caaguazuensis-4/",
      "html": "<p>Larvophile maternal mouthbrooder: the female incubates the larvae in her mouth, while the animals spawn on stones etc. and take care of the eggs like open-breeding cichlids until they hatch.</p>"
    }
  ],
